        "summaryText": "I've read the source files. Here's what I found:\n\n**Current implementation:**\n- `src/tokenizer.mjs` — `createTokenizer()` with `push`/`finish`, plus `parseRows(chunks)`.\n- `src/state.mjs` — `createState`, `feedChar`, `finishState`. Handles plain/quoted/afterQuote modes, CR/LF, and `pendingCR`.\n- `src/assembler.mjs` — `finishField`, `finishRecord`, `drainRows`.\n- `src/line.mjs` — `consumeLine` (only finishes a record on `\\r` or `\\n`).\n- `src/escape.mjs` — `syntax(code)` helper.\n- `src/item-schema.mjs` — `validateItemRow` (2 columns, non-empty id).\n- `src/consumers/read-items.mjs` — `readItems`.\n- `src/consumers/count-items.mjs` — `countItems`.\n- `src/slug.mjs`, `src/checksum.mjs` — unrelated helpers.\n- `public.test.mjs` — tests for ordinary rows, quoted commas, split CRLF, doubled quotes, and the helpers.\n\n**Observations / potential issues:**\n1. `feedChar` sets `state.pendingCR` nowhere — `pendingCR` is initialized `false` and never set to `true`, so the `pendingCR` branch in `feedChar` and the `BARE_CR` check in `finishState` are dead code. CRLF handling currently works only because `consumeLine` treats both `\\r` and `\\n` as record terminators, which means a lone `\\r` also ends a record (and a `\\r\\n` would end two records — but `finishRecord` resets `touched`, so the second is suppressed).\n2. `consumeLine` ignores its `char` argument's distinction and always finishes a record for either `\\r` or `\\n`.\n\nI don't yet have a stated task or failing test to act on. Could you tell me what change you'd like made (e.g., a specific bug to fix, a new feature, or a failing test to satisfy)?",
